    description: "WHAT. resolve_deferred_symbol_refs tells same-named handlers apart by the module the reference names (metadata.module_name, or the qualifier of a dotted name). Since PR #2326 the Python analyzer writes module_name for a route handler its import walk could not find. The other eight analyzers that emit usage contexts (js_ts, go, ruby, php, elixir, rust, clojure, swift) write no module_name, so for them a tie among same-named handlers falls to the reference's own file and then to position, unless the handler name itself is dotted.\n\nASK. Per analyzer: record the module (or file) the handler reference's import names, where the language has one. JS/TS first: an Express router file imports its handlers by relative path, which names the file exactly.\n\nNOT CHECKED. How many usage contexts per language name a key that several symbols hold (on pretix src/pretix it was 76 of 586, all Python).\n\nFound during PR #2326 (2026-11-22). Evidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/three_pr_plan_11222026/pr1/RESULTS.md section 2."  # 8cc5
